        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues (1 and 2) with one change: I reworded the comment at `json.ts:227` so it no longer uses a TODO marker.\n\nThe comment explains a deliberate choice. The `extensions` filter is left out of the `fileOpen` call because a WebKit bug (https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=34442) stops iOS users from opening `.excalidraw` files when a filter is set. Nothing in this code can complete that \"task\", since the fix depends on WebKit. So I followed the rule's help text (\"Remove or rephrase this comment\") and turned it into a note that says the behaviour is intentional. It keeps the bug link, the reason, and the filter to put back once the bug is fixed (`extensions: [\"json\", \"excalidraw\", \"png\", \"svg\"]`).\n\nOnly the comment changed, so runtime behaviour is the same. I couldn't re-run the linter because the command needed approval, which can't be given in this run. The new text contains no TODO, FIXME or similar keyword, so neither rule should fire again.",
